comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T19:42:35.002Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-07: searched all PM statuses for GH-931, dist/cli.js, is_pm_command, linked-test command classification, and false PM context. Open pm-e97jyf owns broad direct-versus-linked execution-context parity and closed pm-oslr owns the SDK execution primitive; neither owns this executable-identity false positive, so this focused child issue is distinct and typed to both."
  "2026-08-07T19:42:58.650Z","harness:codex","GitHub report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/931; backlink comment: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/931#issuecomment-5221326380."
  "2026-08-08T16:46:56.777Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence (2026-08-08): full release pipeline reached the pre-commit hosted-review boundary after all local gates passed. Exact coverage: 460 files, 7072 tests, statements 50283/50283, branches 36738/36738, functions 10330/10330, lines 48684/48684. Static quality/docstrings, docs/skills, SDK surface, package boundary/parity, token/context/retrieval/tracker/security/version, packed npx (13 packages), and 88-command temporary package-first dogfood all passed. Manual packed external acceptance also passed all-status duplicates, 13 unique package rows with aliases, SDK direction-independent merge, package-manage output resolution, merge install, and health classification. The remaining greptile gate refusal is expected before a reviewable commit: no committed code changes to review against main."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T16:49:43.511Z","harness:codex",Executable suffixes are not identities; linked-test context routing must establish package ownership before applying pm-specific sandbox and mismatch policy.
